  "details": "When performing a System.Object.equals() comparison on TokenType values (as might happen if you do `if (token.Type == TokenType.Error)`), two GC allocations seem to occur (in world SDK 3.10.3 - I can't confirm if this happens in-client, but if there's a difference here it makes it effectively impossible to optimize Udon scripts to reduce GC hitching).\n\nSee attached screenshot - I have some harmony hooks in to apply profiler markers around extern calls. If you need the harmony hooks for comparison, here they are: https://gist.github.com/bdunderscore/c325c6e1fc8d29a6c501c6eda09ca0fc",
